  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "For a real number \\(x,\\) define \\(\\heartsuit(x)\\) to be the average of \\(x\\) and \\(x^2.\\) What is the value of the following expression? \\[\\heartsuit(1)+\\heartsuit(2)+\\heartsuit(3)\\]",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(20\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "10"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2010-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\[ \\heartsuit(1) = \\dfrac{1 + 1^2}{2} = 1, \\] \\[ \\heartsuit(2) = \\dfrac{2 + 2^2}{2} = 3, \\] and \\[ \\heartsuit(3) = \\dfrac{3 + 3^2}{2} = 6. \\]\n\nThen \\[ 1 + 3 + 6 = 10. \\]\n\nThus, C is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Evaluate \\(\\heartsuit(1),\\heartsuit(2),\\heartsuit(3)\\) separately",
        "\\(\\heartsuit(x)=\\dfrac{x+x^2}{2}\\)"
      ],
